cases
requirement	case	module	access program	error	reason	output	diagnostic	assertion
view.1	1	void-os	void-os			true		with no operand the view gives the overview of every input
view.2	1	void-os	void-os			true		with an input's name as the one operand the view gives that input's days
view.3	1	void-os	void-os			true		with a position as the third operand the view gives the details of that value
view.5	1	void-os	void-os			true		the view marks no value communicated
view.6	1	void-os	void-os		no input /no/such<LF>	false	true	an input that does not exist is refused with the reason no input, a space, and the operand, nothing on standard output
view.9	1	void-os	void-os		too many operands<LF>	false	true	more than three operands are refused as too many operands, nothing on standard output
view.8	1	void-os	void-os			true		with --filter the view keeps the level's records for which the filter holds, then lays it out and writes it
